      "properties": {
        "release_year": 1965,
        "content_rating": "G",
        "description": "The Sound of Music (1965), directed by Robert Wise and starring Julie Andrews, Christopher Plummer, and Eleanor Parker, is a sprawling period musical drama adapted from the stage musical about the von Trapp family. Set in 1930s Austria, it follows a postulant sent to be governess to seven children who brings music and warmth to a strict household, sparks a romance with the widowed captain, and ultimately helps the family confront rising political danger. The film blends large-scale musical numbers, sentimental family drama, and historical biographical elements to explore themes of love, duty, faith, and escape, delivered in a warm, nostalgic tone."
